<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-20--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-20: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.36";
    dc:description "A reinforcement test with yoked controls would cleanly confirm or refute trainability of a morphological outcome. The source paper marks the experiment as not yet done, and public follow-up through 2026 is proposal and framework rather than a deposited training result. The necessary measurements are still to be collected.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Deliver a nutrient, endorphin, or shock contingency contingent on an anatomical or expression state, against a yoked non-contingent control; trainability holds if only the contingent group moves toward the rewarded morphology.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Later discussions and proposed reinforcement protocols have not released such an outcome dataset.", "No public experiment pairs contingent reward or punishment with a morphological endpoint.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.72"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.36"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
